One mutation was written, found to be equivalent, and dropped rather than counted. Removing
the caller's `|| exit 1` after `fingerprint "${tree_before}"` leaves the run failing for the
same reason, because the script runs under `set -e` and a bare failing function call already
ends it. The fixture still asserts the message and the exit status; the mutant that would have
distinguished the two does not exist. That is written up in
`docs/verification/verify-in-docker-entry-blindness-2026-10-04.log`.

== 9. Reproduce it

    $ python3 scripts/ci/test-check-lab-coverage.py
    $ python3 scripts/ci/check-lab-coverage.py
    $ python3 scripts/ci/check-lab-coverage.py --list

The gate asks nothing of the network and nothing of Docker, so it runs on any clone. To see
the staleness rule bite, move a ledger row's date back 31 days and re-run it:

    $ python3 - <<'PY'
    import pathlib
    p = pathlib.Path("scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv")
    p.write_text(p.read_text().replace("2026-10-04", "2026-09-03"))
    PY
    $ python3 scripts/ci/check-lab-coverage.py
    check-lab-coverage: FAIL (4 problem(s))
      scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv:6: scripts/install-sh-in-docker.sh last ran on 2026-09-03, 31 days ago, past the 30-day budget; re-run it and update the row: bash scripts/install-sh-in-docker.sh 2>&1 | tee docs/verification/<dated log>
      scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv:7: scripts/npm-install-in-docker.sh last ran on 2026-09-03, 31 days ago, past the 30-day budget; re-run it and update the row: bash scripts/npm-install-in-docker.sh 2>&1 | tee docs/verification/<dated log>
      scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv:8: transcript docs/verification/verify-in-docker-full-a04e91a7-2026-09-03.log is not tracked; a log that exists only on one machine is not evidence for a commit
      scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv:8: scripts/verify-in-docker.sh last ran on 2026-09-03, 31 days ago, past the 30-day budget; re-run it and update the row: bash scripts/verify-in-docker.sh 2>&1 | tee docs/verification/<dated log>
    $ git checkout -- scripts/ci/docker-labs.tsv

The third problem is the transcript rule firing alongside the date rule: the rewrite changed
the date inside the transcript's filename too, and a log that is not tracked cannot vouch for
a commit. Both are errors, and the gate reports every one rather than the first.

The labs themselves need Docker; two of them also build the workspace:

    $ bash scripts/web-deployment-in-docker.sh
    $ bash scripts/remote-acceptance-in-docker.sh
    $ bash scripts/install-sh-in-docker.sh
    $ bash scripts/npm-install-in-docker.sh
